  "regressions": [
    "Fourteen fresh native snapshots include every start frame 27 through 38 plus initial/final starts.",
    "Seven native restart tests reject corrupt trees, pairs, counters, contact graphs, past/future trace writes and buffer guards; validation does not mutate captured inputs.",
    "Existing brute-force restart checks and registry/inventory drift checks remain required."
  ],
  "differences": [
    "The 120-frame LBVH triangle comparison remains unresolved: its transient angular-velocity difference reaches 0.139234, while the same-input frame-36 restart is within the existing strict policy. Several surrounding same-input restarts exceed strict output tolerances by small amounts and require explicit numerical classification and current target evidence.",
    "Only the already-reset frontier length is normalized for input-schema checking; all captured kernel inputs and guard words are preserved.",
